UnitCrosschain::bridgeToken
├── given a lite deployment with no interchain account router
│   ├── when the recipient is the zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with CommandDisabled
│   └── when a direct recipient is supplied on the lite deployment
│       └── it should bridge to the direct recipient without the interchain account router
├── when the recipient is the metarouter
│   └── it should revert with InvalidRecipient
├── when a direct recipient is combined with a custom interchain account configuration
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInterchainAccountConfig
├── when a direct recipient is supplied for an ERC20
│   ├── it should not read the interchain account router
│   ├── it should track the token
│   ├── it should approve the bridge for the resolved amount
│   ├── it should bridge the token to the direct recipient
│   └── it should clear the bridge approval
├── when an erc20 bridge names a message fee above the available native balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the native asset
├── when the interchain account configuration names an ISM without a router
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInterchainAccountConfig
├── when a custom interchain account configuration uses the zero ISM
│   ├── it should derive the recipient with the custom router and zero ISM
│   └── it should not require an enrolled router for the domain
├── when a custom interchain account configuration is used for an ERC20
│   ├── it should derive the recipient with the custom router and non-zero ISM
│   ├── it should track the token
│   ├── it should approve the bridge for the resolved amount
│   ├── it should bridge the token to the custom-derived recipient
│   └── it should clear the bridge approval
├── given the token is the zero address
│   ├── when the native spend is an absolute amount
│   │   ├── it should resolve the spend against the available native balance
│   │   ├── it should derive _recipient from the interchain account router with the logical sender as salt
│   │   ├── it should forward the whole spend as value to transferRemote with the delivery amount
│   │   └── it should neither approve nor track the native route
│   ├── when the native spend takes the full available balance in pips
│   │   ├── it should resolve the full available native balance
│   │   ├── it should forward the whole spend as value to transferRemote with the delivery amount
│   │   └── it should neither approve nor track the native route
│   └── when the router holds native predating the batch
│       ├── it should resolve only the batch introduced native
│       ├── it should ignore _messageFee
│       ├── it should forward the whole spend as value to transferRemote with the delivery amount
│       ├── it should leave the pre batch balance untouched
│       └── it should clear the transient execution slots at closure
└── given the token is not the zero address
    ├── when the destination domain is not registered
    │   └── it should revert with UnregisteredDomain
    └── given the destination domain is registered
        ├── when the bridge does not manage the token
        │   └── it should revert with BridgeTokenMismatch
        └── given the bridge manages the token
            ├── when the resolved amount is zero
            │   └── it should revert with ZeroAmount
            ├── when a pips spend resolves to zero
            │   └── it should revert with ZeroAmount
            ├── when an amount spend of the native mirror token exceeds the batch native less the message fee
            │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the token
            ├── when a lower decimals mirror spend exceeds the batch native less the converted message fee
            │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the token
            ├── when a converted message fee consumes the whole batch mirror balance
            │   └── it should revert with ZeroAmount
            ├── when a pips spend message fee equals the batch native
            │   └── it should revert with ZeroAmount
            └── given the resolved amount is positive
                ├── when a pips spend names a max fee above the denominator
                │   └── it should revert with InvalidPips
                ├── when the quoted total is below the amount
                │   └── it should revert with InvalidBridgeQuote
                └── given the quoted total covers the amount
                    ├── when the token fee exceeds the max token fee
                    │   └── it should revert with TokenFeeExceedsMax
                    ├── when a pips spend fee exceeds the max token fee
                    │   └── it should revert with TokenFeeExceedsMax
                    ├── when using a known ceil rounded pip fee at the maximum
                    │   └── it should accept the hand computed ceiling fee boundary
                    ├── when using a known ceil rounded pip fee above the maximum
                    │   └── it should revert with TokenFeeExceedsMax
                    ├── when the token fee consumes the whole amount
                    │   └── it should revert with TokenFeeExceedsAmount
                    ├── when a pips spend fee consumes the whole amount
                    │   └── it should revert with TokenFeeExceedsAmount
                    ├── when the route charges no fee
                    │   ├── it should track _token
                    │   ├── it should derive _recipient from the interchain account router with the logical sender as salt
                    │   ├── it should approve _bridge for the resolved amount
                    │   ├── it should call transferRemote on _bridge with _recipient and the whole amount forwarding _messageFee
                    │   └── it should clear the _bridge approval
                    ├── when the spend selects a pips proportion
                    │   ├── it should track _token
                    │   ├── it should derive _recipient from the interchain account router with the logical sender as salt
                    │   ├── it should approve _bridge for the resolved proportion
                    │   ├── it should call transferRemote on _bridge with _recipient and the proportion less the quoted fee forwarding _messageFee
                    │   └── it should clear the _bridge approval
                    ├── when a full pips spend selects the native mirror token
                    │   ├── it should resolve the batch native less the message fee
                    │   ├── it should approve _bridge for the reduced amount
                    │   ├── it should call transferRemote on _bridge with _recipient and the reduced amount less the quoted fee forwarding _messageFee
                    │   ├── it should clear the _bridge approval
                    │   └── it should refund the unresolved batch native to the caller at closure
                    ├── when a mirror amount spend equals the batch native less the message fee
                    │   ├── it should resolve the spend at the fee reserved batch balance
                    │   ├── it should approve _bridge for the amount
                    │   ├── it should call transferRemote on _bridge with _recipient and the amount forwarding _messageFee
                    │   ├── it should clear the _bridge approval
                    │   └── it should refund the unpulled batch native to the caller at closure
                    ├── when the bridge pulls the approved mirror amount
                    │   ├── it should call transferRemote on the bridge with the resolved amount forwarding _messageFee
                    │   ├── it should leave no closing refund for the caller
                    │   └── it should leave the pre batch native with the router at closure
                    ├── when the bridge pulls the approved six decimal mirror amount
                    │   ├── it should call transferRemote on the bridge with the converted raw unit amount forwarding _messageFee
                    │   ├── it should refund the fee reservation and flooring remainders to the caller at closure
                    │   └── it should leave the fractional pre batch native with the router at closure
                    ├── when the route charges a fee within the maximum
                    │   ├── it should track _token
                    │   ├── it should derive _recipient from the interchain account router with the logical sender as salt
                    │   ├── it should approve _bridge for the resolved amount
                    │   ├── it should call transferRemote on _bridge with _recipient and the amount less the quoted fee forwarding _messageFee
                    │   └── it should clear the _bridge approval
                    └── when the quote spreads the token total across entries
                        ├── it should track _token
                        ├── it should derive _recipient from the interchain account router with the logical sender as salt
                        ├── it should approve _bridge for the resolved amount
                        ├── it should call transferRemote on _bridge with _recipient and the amount less the summed fee ignoring entries in other denominations forwarding _messageFee
                        └── it should clear the _bridge approval

UnitCrosschain::executeCrosschain
├── given a lite deployment with no interchain account router
│   └── it should revert with CommandDisabled
├── when the message fee exceeds the available native balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the native asset
├── when the interchain account configuration names an ISM without a router
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInterchainAccountConfig
├── when a custom interchain account configuration uses the zero ISM
│   ├── it should dispatch with the custom router and zero ISM
│   └── it should not read the enrolled router or ISM
├── when a custom interchain account configuration uses a nonzero ISM
│   ├── it should dispatch with the custom router and ISM
│   └── it should not read the enrolled router or ISM
├── when the destination domain is not registered
│   └── it should revert with UnregisteredDomain
└── given the destination domain is registered
    ├── when the hook metadata is shorter than the refund offset
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidHookMetadata
    └── given the hook metadata carries a refund address
        ├── when the hook metadata stops before the fee token field
        │   └── it should call callRemoteCommitReveal with _commitment and the logical sender as salt forwarding _messageFee
        ├── when the hook metadata names the zero address as fee token
        │   └── it should call callRemoteCommitReveal with _commitment and the logical sender as salt forwarding _messageFee
        ├── when the hook metadata names a fee token
        │   ├── it should track the metadata fee token
        │   ├── it should approve the interchain account router for _tokenFee
        │   ├── it should call callRemoteCommitReveal with _commitment and the logical sender as salt forwarding _messageFee
        │   └── it should clear the metadata fee token approval
        ├── when the hook metadata names the native mirror token beyond the batch native
        │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the fee token
        ├── when the native mirror fee grant equals the batch native less the message fee
        │   ├── it should approve the interchain account router for the fee grant
        │   ├── it should call callRemoteCommitReveal with _commitment and the logical sender as salt forwarding _messageFee
        │   ├── it should clear the metadata fee token approval
        │   └── it should leave the stranded pre batch native with the router at closure
        ├── when the hook metadata names a lower decimals mirror beyond the converted batch native
        │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the fee token
        └── when the command allows revert
            └── it should call callRemoteCommitReveal with the logical sender as salt from the self called child frame

UnitCrosschain::redeem
├── when the deployment has no leaf voter
│   └── it should revert with CommandDisabled
├── when the recipient is the metarouter
│   └── it should revert with InvalidRecipient
├── when the message fee exceeds the available native balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the native asset
├── when the payer is the user and the spend mode is pips
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSpendMode
├── when the payer is the user and the spend mode is an amount
│   ├── it should pull the amount from the logical sender
│   └── it should call redeem on the leaf voter with the measured delta
├── when the payer is internal and the spend mode is an amount
│   ├── it should track the receipt token
│   ├── it should call redeem on the leaf voter with the amount _recipient and _gasLimit forwarding _messageFee
│   ├── it should name itself as the refund recipient for a zero input
│   ├── it should return the unredeemed receipt balance to the caller at closure
│   └── it should clear the transient execution slots at closure
├── when the payer is internal and the spend mode is pips
│   ├── it should track the receipt token
│   ├── it should call redeem on the leaf voter with the resolved proportion _recipient and _gasLimit forwarding _messageFee
│   ├── it should return the unredeemed receipt balance to the caller at closure
│   └── it should clear the transient execution slots at closure
├── when the payer is internal and the spend consumes the whole receipt balance
│   ├── it should call redeem on the leaf voter with the full balance
│   ├── it should not transfer the receipt token at closure
│   └── it should clear the transient execution slots at closure
└── when the refund recipient is not the zero address
    └── it should call redeem on the leaf voter with the supplied refund recipient
